#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Link fields of the content type"
msgstr ""

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Fields of your content types that hold a link, one per line, as the address of a link. Taken over, not translated; an internal link points at the translation of its target where there is one. Links inside blocks are found on their own."
msgstr ""

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Link keys inside blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Which keys of a block hold a link to other content. The default is what Plone itself watches for link integrity, plus the key an object browser writes. A block type of your own may need its own keys named here."
msgstr ""

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Prose keys inside blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Which keys of a block hold text to translate. Only the key tells a sentence apart from a token the front end reads, so a block type of your own needs its own keys named here, or its text stays in the source language."
msgstr ""


