#: ../helpers/field_selection.py
msgid "Page content"
msgstr "Page content"

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Fields per content type"
msgstr "Fields per content type"

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Sets per content type which fields go along into the translation. Only fields filled in on the page count. Whether a field is translated or taken over as it is follows from the kind of field; a field with values in the metadata mapping goes through the mapping."
msgstr "Sets per content type which fields go along into the translation. Only fields filled in on the page count. Whether a field is translated or taken over as it is follows from the kind of field; a field with values in the metadata mapping goes through the mapping."

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Fields never translated"
msgstr "Fields never translated"

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Fields that never go into a translation and are not listed per content type: they belong to the object, not to its language. Named as in the schema, one per line, for every content type."
msgstr "Fields that never go into a translation and are not listed per content type: they belong to the object, not to its language. Named as in the schema, one per line, for every content type."

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Fields always translated"
msgstr "Fields always translated"

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Fields that always go into a translation and cannot be left out per content type; they come first in the list. Named as in the schema, one per line. The main field of a type, as the image of an image, always goes along too."
msgstr "Fields that always go into a translation and cannot be left out per content type; they come first in the list. Named as in the schema, one per line. The main field of a type, as the image of an image, always goes along too."

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Fields taken over unchanged"
msgstr "Fields taken over unchanged"

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Fields taken over as they are where their kind would have them translated: text that is no prose, as an address or a project number. Named as in the schema, one per line, for every content type. A field still only goes along when it is chosen for the content type."
msgstr "Fields taken over as they are where their kind would have them translated: text that is no prose, as an address or a project number. Named as in the schema, one per line, for every content type. A field still only goes along when it is chosen for the content type."

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "DeepL glossary IDs"
msgstr "DeepL glossary IDs"

#: ../registry/translation.py
msgid "Optional, one ID per direction: a DeepL glossary is always for one language pair. It sets how terms are translated, as proper names, the names of institutes or fixed titles. The glossaries are kept in the DeepL account; here only their IDs are named (e.g. 4b1b0f1c-9d7a-4b6e-9a0a-3f2c8f0e51d7). For the keywords the metadata mapping counts instead."
msgstr "Optional, one ID per direction: a DeepL glossary is always for one language pair. It sets how terms are translated, as proper names, the names of institutes or fixed titles. The glossaries are kept in the DeepL account; here only their IDs are named (e.g. 4b1b0f1c-9d7a-4b6e-9a0a-3f2c8f0e51d7). For the keywords the metadata mapping counts instead."

